    "text": "Kerbel Lighthouse 0 Skip to content GALLERY THE LIGHTHOUSE RATES AND CONDITIONS CONTACT AND PRACTICAL INFORMATION WHAT TO DO AROUND THE HISTORY OF THE LIGHTHOUSE LIFE AT THE LIGHTHOUSE PRESS AND MEDIA FAQ Book your stay Open the menu Close the menu GALLERY THE LIGHTHOUSE RATES AND CONDITIONS CONTACT AND PRACTICAL INFORMATION WHAT TO DO AROUND THE HISTORY OF THE LIGHTHOUSE LIFE AT THE LIGHTHOUSE PRESS AND MEDIA FAQ Book your stay Open the menu Close the menu GALLERY THE LIGHTHOUSE RATES AND CONDITIONS CONTACT AND PRACTICAL INFORMATION WHAT TO DO AROUND THE HISTORY OF THE LIGHTHOUSE LIFE AT THE LIGHTHOUSE PRESS AND MEDIA FAQ Book your stay Scroll down To access availability and book, click below: Availability and reservations An exceptional place. \"This landscape has been familiar to me for 47 years and in all kinds of weather, in storms, in thunderstorms, in fact in all the weather you can see from 30 metres up, and at all hours of the night and day. When there was snow, it was magical to see all of Port-Louis and Gâvres covered in snow. I would sometimes spend an hour on the stairs despite the intense cold just to enjoy the snowy landscape...\" Throughout her life, Honorine Le Guen, France's first female lighthouse keeper, looked after the Kerbel Lighthouse daily to guide sailors entering Lorient harbour. Today, although improvements in navigation systems have made it obsolete, the Kerbel Lighthouse, always a pioneer, has been transformed into the only lighthouse in France habitable at the top, offering each of us the possibility of following in Honorine's footsteps... Discover the Kerbel Lighthouse GALLERY EXPLORE THE ENTIRE GALLERY Slide 1 Slide 1 (current slide) Slide 2 Slide 2 (current slide) Slide 3 Slide 3 (current slide) Slide 4 Slide 4 (current slide) Slide 5 Slide 5 (current slide) THE LIGHTHOUSE The keeper's house The keeper's house bears its name because it was the home of its keeper from 1913, the date of the Kerbel lighthouse's inauguration, to 1989, the date its lens was extinguished. It has now been completely refurbished to offer you optimum comfort while retaining the spirit of its original occupants... EXPLORE The studio on top of the lighthouse The Kerbel lighthouse is the only lighthouse in France that is habitable at the top. An architectural feat has enabled a studio to replace the lantern that once guided sailors at a height of 25 metres, offering a 360° panorama stretching almost to infinity. EXPLORE The Oil Room Formerly used for storage, it housed the oil powering the lantern of the Kerbel lighthouse, before its electrification in 1932. Today, transformed into an outbuilding, it is no longer oil that you will come to look for, but rather the comfort of a peaceful night at the foot of the lighthouse. EXPLORE SWIMMING POOL SAUNA GARDEN The outdoor space... The garden of the Kerbel Lighthouse covers more than 1,000m2 and allows you to take advantage of the slightest ray of sunshine: breakfast on the garden furniture, devour "
