    "text": "Château de Mercuès - Cahors Skip to main content Our wine trips All our wine trips Destination Alsace Beaujolais Bordeaux Burgundy Catalonia Champagne Cognac Corsica Jura Languedoc-Roussillon Paris Provence Savoy South-West Loire Valley Rhone Valley Type of stay Self-drive tours Wine tours Tailor-made Wine & food Wine Romance History & Culture Luxury Wine Tours Off the beaten tracks Corporate Our featured stay Food and Wine Tour in Bordeaux east About us About us Our Team Client testimonials Plan my trip France's Wine Routes Visit French Vineyards Tasting French Wines French Cuisine Redeem my stay menu close arrow_back Mobile menu Mobile menu --> Our wine trips About us Plan my trip Redeem my stay +33 (0)1 85 46 00 09 Our featured stay Food and Wine Tour in Bordeaux east Destination Alsace Beaujolais Bordeaux Burgundy Catalonia Champagne Cognac Corsica Jura Languedoc-Roussillon Paris Provence Savoy South-West Loire Valley Rhone Valley Type of stay Self-drive tours Wine tours Tailor-made Wine & food Wine Romance History & Culture Luxury Wine Tours Off the beaten tracks Corporate All our wine trips About us Our Team Client testimonials France's Wine Routes Visit French Vineyards Tasting French Wines French Cuisine Vinotrip +33 (0)1 85 46 00 09 Need help with your booking? Our team is available Monday to Friday, from 9:30 am to 12:30 pm and from 1:30 pm to 6:00 pm. +33 (0)1 85 46 00 09 Sign in Château de Mercuès Rue du Château, 46090 Mercuès Carefully selected wineries and estates Charming places to stay Trusted local partners Tried-and-tested experiences Staying at Château de Mercuès Perched on a hill overlooking the Lot Valley and the Cahors vineyards, Château de Mercuès is a 13th-century castle with a rich and eventful history. Once the summer residence of the Count-Bishops of Cahors, it played a role during the Hundred Years’ War and the Wars of Religion, suffering occupation, looting and fire over the centuries. After passing through several hands and periods of neglect and restoration, the château was acquired in 1983 by Georges Vigouroux, a Cahors winemaker captivated by this exceptional place. He undertook major renovation work to restore Mercuès to its former glory and bring it back into the prestigious Relais & Châteaux collection. Weekend around the city of Cahors A beautiful medieval castle near Cahors, tastings of the Malbec (the caracteristic grape variety of the region), a gastronomic dinner: a true wine romance! South-West 5.0/5 (1 reviews) Cahors wine weekend Château de Mercuès + Michelin-starred dinner + AOC Cahors + Romantic stay 2 days / 1 night from €490 pp Restaurants and rooms of the Château This magnificent medieval castle, which is also a vineyard estate, offers you today to stay in one of their 24 rooms, divided into several categories, and their 6 suites as luxurious as unusual, all with an impregnable view on the vineyard of The valley or on the garden of the property. Concerning its food offerings, you must know that Châ"
