    "description": "Escape to Domaine des Etangs, a luxury French countryside resort in Massignac, blending timeless charm, refined design, and five-star hospitality.",
    "text": "Domaine Des Etangs in Massignac, France | Auberge Collection Skip To Main Content Skip To Footer FR: 05 45 61 85 00 | US Toll Free: +1 877.496.0660 Book now Stay Cottages Dine Wellbeing Experiences Events & Weddings Art Offers Gallery Getting Here Gift Cards Family Journal Hotel Information Itineraries Press Careers Philanthropy Arrive Depart Sep, 2026 26 Sep, 2026 28 Check Availability Condé Nast Traveler Gold List 2024 and the Readers Choice #1 Hotel in France Awarded 2 MICHELIN Keys in 2024 & 2025 A 13th-Century French Château Imbued with Nature's Artistic Soul Nestled within 2,500 forested acres (1,000 hectares), Domaine des Etangs is a magnificent stone château where balance is found through art, nature, and the time-honored traditions of French country living. Built over 700 years ago by the knights of Chasteignier de la Roche-Posay, this storybook castle is a serene retreat devoted to l’art de vivre, past and present. Resting beside the tranquil ponds that inspired its name, the Domaine offers nature-inspired guest rooms, charming farmhouse cottages, the One-Michelin-starred Restaurant Dyades, the award-winning Le Moulin spa, and an art collection woven seamlessly into its landscape—each element embodying the harmony symbolized by its dragonfly emblem. Reserve Awarded 2 MICHELIN Keys in 2024 & 2025 A 13th-Century French Château Imbued with Nature's Artistic Soul Nestled within 2,500 forested acres (1,000 hectares), Domaine des Etangs is a magnificent stone château where balance is found through art, nature, and the time-honored traditions of French country living. Built over 700 years ago by the knights of Chasteignier de la Roche-Posay, this storybook castle is a serene retreat devoted to l’art de vivre, past and present. Resting beside the tranquil ponds that inspired its name, the Domaine offers nature-inspired guest rooms, charming farmhouse cottages, the One-Michelin-starred Restaurant Dyades, the award-winning Le Moulin spa, and an art collection woven seamlessly into its landscape—each element embodying the harmony symbolized by its dragonfly emblem. Reserve Stay Between Heaven and Earth From the château with its seven suites, vast attic games room, and Gallo-Roman-inspired thermal baths, to the six Metairie cottages and The Longère’s four rustic suites, untouched original materials and witty art and experiences give the Domaine its curiosity and sense of discovery. Guestrooms Suites Cottages All Accommodations accommodations Farm to Table Few can claim a farm-to-table journey as authentic and ephemeral as Domaine des Etangs. At the heart of our kitchen lies the potager, where each vegetable and herb is cultivated in harmony with nature’s rhythms. Dyades, the Domaine’s One-Michelin-starred restaurant, draws endless inspiration from this garden and the region’s finest ingredients, seamlessly blending tradition with innovation, simplicity with sophistication. Learn More Farm to Table Few can claim a farm-to-table journey as authentic "
