    "description": "Explore Megève in a different way: authentic mountain village, gastronomy, culture, infrastructure and the art of living all year round.",
    "text": "Discover Megève - Megève Tourism Skip to content Are you in the right place? Your browser language appears to be different from the language of the site you are viewing. To provide you with the best possible experience, we invite you to select the language in which you wish to view our site. English French Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Open the menu Discover See more Previous Discover Village of Megève Gastronomy Facilities Blog To ski See more Previous To ski Winter sports Ski station Package purchases Family skiing Ski schools Equipment rental Activities See more Previous Activities Outdoor Indoor Well-being & relaxation Aquatic Culture & Discovery aerial Restaurants & Nightlife Plan my stay See more Previous Plan my stay Accommodations Access and mobility Accessible station Family resort Practical Info See more Previous Practical Info Live news Our booklets Megève mobile app Our commitments Shops & services Webcams Weather Events FR FR Open the search bar Events Live Megeve Commune Discover Megeve Home / Discover Megeve Nestled in the heart of the Alps, just a stone's throw from Mont Blanc, Megève is much more than just a ski resort: it's a way of life. With its majestic nature, authentic heritage, modern infrastructure, and unique atmosphere, the village reveals an unexpected richness every season. Why visit Megève? Located in Haute-Savoie, in the heart of the French Alps, Megève is a mountain destination renowned for its authentic village, heritage, gastronomy, and numerous activities in both summer and winter. Facing the Mont Blanc massif, the resort appeals to ski enthusiasts, families, hiking aficionados, nature lovers, and travelers seeking a refined Alpine lifestyle. Megève stands out for its identity as a true mountain village, alive all year round. Between cobbled streets, traditional chalets, renowned restaurants, cultural events, wellness areas and vast natural spaces, the destination offers a complete experience in every season. Just an hour from Geneva, Megève is also an ideal destination for a weekend or a stay in the heart of the Alps. The village of Megève The history of Megève dates back to the Middle Ages. But it was at the beginning of the 20th century, under the leadership of Baroness Noémie de Rothschild, that the village took a new turn: becoming a chic alternative to Swiss resorts like Saint-Moritz. Thanks to this bold vision, Megève became the first French ski resort designed for refined, family-friendly tourism. The wooden chalets, sculpted balconies, calvaries, fountains, and cobbled streets bear witness to this rich past. But beyond the stones, it is the faces, the local families, the artisans, and the elders who give Megève its living memory. A precious heritage that the village protects and promotes, so that every visitor can feel its soul. History & Heritage Neighborhoods Village of Megève Kitchen & Lifestyle In Megève, every meal is an invitation to discovery. From Michelin-starred restaurants to family-run "
