    "text": "Village of Megève - Megève Tourism Skip to content Are you in the right place? Your browser language appears to be different from the language of the site you are viewing. To provide you with the best possible experience, we invite you to select the language in which you wish to view our site. English French Italian Portuguese Russian Spanish Open the menu Discover See more Previous Discover Village of Megève Gastronomy Facilities Blog To ski See more Previous To ski Winter sports Ski station Package purchases Family skiing Ski schools Equipment rental Activities See more Previous Activities Outdoor Indoor Well-being & relaxation Aquatic Culture & Discovery aerial Restaurants & Nightlife Plan my stay See more Previous Plan my stay Accommodations Access and mobility Accessible station Family resort Practical Info See more Previous Practical Info Live news Our booklets Megève mobile app Our commitments Shops & services Webcams Weather Events FR FR Open the search bar Events Live Village of Megève Home / Discover Megeve / Village of Megève Nestled in the heart of the French Alps, the village of Megève captivates visitors with its preserved heritage, authentic atmosphere, and unique way of life. With its cobbled streets, lively squares, traditional chalets, elegant boutiques, and views of the surrounding mountains, Megève is one of the most iconic villages in Haute-Savoie. Unlike many resorts built around skiing, Megève is first and foremost a true mountain village that thrives year-round. Its historic center invites leisurely strolls, while its shops, restaurants, art galleries, events, and entertainment offer a rich experience in every season. History and heritage From farming village to iconic ski resort, Megève has survived the centuries while preserving its soul and authenticity. Its typical architecture, its historic church and its still deeply rooted traditions make it a place where history meets elegance. Discover how Megève has become a must-see destination while preserving its unique heritage. Dive into the history of the village The must-sees of the village of Megève During a stay in Megève, several places are worth visiting: The Church of Saint John the Baptist and its iconic bell tower The cobbled streets of the historic center The Road to Calvary The lively village squares Traditional chalets and architectural heritage Art galleries and cultural spaces The districts of Mont d'Arbois, Rochebrune and Jaillet Markets and events organized throughout the year These places allow you to discover all the richness of the heritage and the art of living in Megevan. The districts of Megève Megève reveals itself through its districts, each with its own atmosphere and character. From the historic charm of the village center with its cobbled streets to the exceptional panoramas of Mont d'Arbois, passing through the calm of the preserved hamlets, each district tells a unique facet of the resort. Discover the neighborhoods Lake Javen, summer webcam view"
