hotel Solidarity hotel Unusual cottage Unusual guest room Unusual hotel Unusual hotel project Youth hostel Hotels-insolites.com > France > Aquitaine > Unusual hotel Périgord > Le Moulin du Roc Le Moulin du Roc Photos : Source Booking.com Unusual and charming hotel in Périgord Arrival Departure In partnership with Presentation Practical information Bucolic stopover in this authentic 17th-century mill of the Périgord. At the north of Dordogne, nestled in Champagnac de Bélair, this 17th-century mill awaits you for a bucolic and timeless getaway. Built on the Dronne, the river that runs through its park, this mill was producing flour and walnut oil until the 1950s. Patiently restored, the mill saw the opening of a bar and then a restaurant in 1969, before the first rooms welcomed travelers. Today, the 15 rooms and suites are spread across the three parts of the mill, connected by walkways, terraces, and stairs. All the rooms of this 4* establishment are unique, charmingly furnished, and comfortable. Fr"
